# ============================================================
#  ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — TEMPLATE
# ============================================================
#
#  THIS file (.env.example) is safe to commit. It contains no real keys.
#  It exists to show you which variables the app looks for.
#
#  TO USE IT:
#    1. Make a copy of this file in the same folder.
#    2. Name the copy exactly:  .env
#    3. Fill in your real values in the copy.
#
#  The .env file is listed in .gitignore, so your keys will never be
#  uploaded to GitHub.
#
#  IMPORTANT: The app works completely fine WITHOUT this file.
#  With no keys set, it runs on built-in demo data. Supabase is an
#  optional upgrade, not a requirement.
#
#  Note on the word "VITE_": Vite only exposes variables to the app if
#  their name starts with VITE_. That prefix is required, not optional.
# ============================================================


# ---------- SUPABASE (optional — added in the final phase) ----------
#
# WHERE TO GET THESE TWO VALUES:
#   1. Go to https://supabase.com and sign up (free, no card needed).
#   2. Click "New project". Pick any name and any strong database password.
#   3. Wait about 2 minutes for the project to finish setting up.
#   4. In the left sidebar click the gear icon (Project Settings).
#   5. Click "API".
#   6. Copy "Project URL"          -> paste after VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
#   7. Copy the "anon" "public" key -> paste after VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
#
# The "anon public" key is designed to be visible in a browser, so using it
# here is correct and safe. Do NOT use the "service_role" key in this app —
# that one is a secret and must never reach the browser.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=


# ---------- WEATHER ----------
#
# No key is needed. We use Open-Meteo (https://open-meteo.com), which is
# free and requires no sign-up or API key for non-commercial use.
# Nothing to fill in here.
